{"term":"ancestor","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:46e704d6db3c65518e","definition":"One from whom a person is descended, whether on the father's or mother's side, at any distance of time; a progenitor; a forefather; a forebear.","example":"Whether modern, industrial man is less or more warlike than his hunter-gatherer ancestors is impossible to determine. The machine gun is so much more lethal than the bow and arrow that comparisons are meaningless.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["forebear","fore-elder","forefather"],"antonyms":["descendant","afterbear"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["ancestorhood","ancestorial","ancestorism","ancestorship","ancestor spirit","ancestor worship","ancestrula","ancestry","apical ancestor","cenancestor","common ancestor","grandancestor","grandcestor","last universal ancestor","last universal common ancestor","proto-ancestor","protoancestor","trancestor","ur-ancestor"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancestor#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1dc6dc72e1b5375582","definition":"An earlier type; a progenitor.","example":"This fossil animal is regarded as the ancestor of the horse.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["ancestor","antecedent","ascendant","ascendent","forerunner","progenitor"],"antonyms":["descendant","afterbear"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["ancestorhood","ancestorial","ancestorism","ancestorship","ancestor spirit","ancestor worship","ancestrula","ancestry","apical ancestor","cenancestor","common ancestor","grandancestor","grandcestor","last universal ancestor","last universal common ancestor","proto-ancestor","protoancestor","trancestor","ur-ancestor"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancestor#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cdc21c6b187b5a0d96","definition"